# Templ Frontend

Package: `frontend`. One page/feature per file (`students.templ`, `process.templ`).

## Page Structure

Full HTML with shared includes:

```templ
templ Students(data StudentData) {
	<!DOCTYPE html>
	<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<title>Students - Zion English Admin Tool</title>
		<link rel="icon" href={ utils.URL("/static/favicon.ico") }/>
		@GlobalIncludes()
	</head>
	<body>
		<div class="container">
			@HeaderSimple()
			// content
		</div>
	</body>
	</html>
}
```

## View vs API Structs

- Display structs (`StudentData`, `StudentItem`) → define in `.templ` file
- Form/API DTOs → `internal/models`; handlers map between them

## Typed enums in templates

Prefer typed enums over `string` for closed value sets (status, docs status, source, action context, filter kind, pill tone).

- **View struct fields:** `Status`, `DocsStatus`, `Source`, `DeleteFrom`, and similar closed-set fields on `frontend.*` structs use types from `internal/constants` or `frontend` (e.g. `constants.StudentStatus`, `constants.ClassListFilterStatus`, `frontend.ClassActionContext`). Not `string`.
- **Handler boundary:** `cmd/` handlers convert `string` → enum when building view structs (`constants.StudentStatus(row.Status)`). Convert enum → `string` only for HTML attributes, form values, and DB/JSON writes.
- **Templ comparisons:** use enum constants (`data.Status == constants.ClassListFilterConducted`), not literals (`"conducted"`).
- **Dropdowns / filters:** build `<option>` lists from `[]StatusOption` slices in `class_status.go` (see `StudentStatusOptions`, `TeacherFilterStatusOptions`). Do not duplicate hardcoded `<option value="...">` rows.
- **Components:** `@EntityViewNotePanel` takes `PillTone`, not raw `"warning"` / `"info"`. Pill helpers in `pill_kind.go` accept typed status enums.
- **Reference:** `learning_materials.templ` and `TeacherItem.Roles []constants.TeacherRole` show the target pattern.
- **Exception:** raw wire-value strings in `<script>` blocks only (templ does not evaluate Go inside script text).

## Shared Components

| Component | File |
|-----------|------|
| `@GlobalIncludes()` | `global.templ` |
| `@HeaderSimple()` | `header.templ` |
| `@TeacherDropdown()` | `dropdowns.templ` |
| `@ScrHTMX()` | `scripts.templ` |
| `@IconActionLink()` / `@IconActionButton()` | `icons.templ`: use `IconKind` constants, not string literals |
| `@Pill()` / `@StatusPill()` | `pills.templ`: use `PillTone` constants, not string literals |
| `@RatePill()` | `pills.templ`: use for class rate displays (scheduled cards, class tables, modal detail cards) |
| `@TimeRangePill()` | `pills.templ`: use for scheduled class time ranges in cards and lists |
| `@TeacherNameCell()` | `avatar.templ`: avatar + teacher name; use whenever a teacher name is shown |

## Pills

Use `@Pill` and `@StatusPill` from `pills.templ` for status and label badges. All pills share a black border via `--pill-border: 1px solid #000` in `global.templ` (applied to `.pill` and `.status-pill`).

- Do not override pill borders with softer `var(--color-border)` unless a design explicitly requires an exception: the default `--pill-border` already uses `var(--color-border)`.
- Custom pill-shaped UI (e.g. `.lm-tag-pill`, `.class-lm-readonly-pill`, `.class-lm-chip`) must use `border: var(--pill-border)`: do not hardcode border colors.
- Prefer extending `.pill` / `.status-pill` classes over inventing one-off pill styles.

## Rate pills

Use `@RatePill(rate, currency)` from `pills.templ` whenever a class rate is shown in the UI (scheduled class cards, class tables, modal detail cards). Do not render rates as plain text.

Use `@TimeRangePill(timeRange)` for scheduled class time ranges in cards and compact list layouts. Group time, rate, and status pills in a shared flex row (`.day-class-pills`) when they appear together on scheduled class cards.

## Modal dismiss actions

Modal footer **Cancel** / dismiss buttons must use `btn btn-secondary` (same as learning-material form modals). Primary/destructive actions keep `btn` or `btn-danger`.

## Teacher name display

Whenever a teacher name is shown in the UI, render it with `@TeacherNameCell(name, avatar)` from `avatar.templ` (or a list wrapper like `@EntityViewTeacherList`). **Never render a bare teacher name string** in tables, modals, cards, or detail views.

- Populate `AvatarProps` in handlers: `buildTeacherListAvatarProps` (lists/rows), `buildReportTeacherAvatarProps` (report modals), `buildTeacherAvatarProps` (profile/detail).
- View structs that carry a teacher name should also carry `AvatarProps` (e.g. `TeacherAvatar`, `Avatar`).
- Include `@AvatarStyles()` on pages that render teacher names outside `GlobalIncludes` partials that already load avatar CSS.

## Icon actions

Action icon kinds are typed as `IconKind` in [`icon_kind.go`](icon_kind.go). Use `@IconActionLink`, `@IconActionButton`, and `@IconActionSubmit` with `IconKind` constants: never build action buttons in client-side JavaScript.

## SSR over client-side DOM building

Prefer server-side rendering with templ components and HTMX partial fetches over complex inline JavaScript.

**Do:**
- Render rows, lists, buttons, and icons in `.templ` (`@IconActionLink`, `@IconActionButton`, row/list components)
- Load dynamic UI via `hx-get` / `hx-post` to handlers that return HTML fragments (see `handleGetTeacherRow`, `/schedule/partials/list`, `/classes/partials/rows`, `/reports/partials/rows`)
- Map DB/API data to view structs in handlers; keep templates declarative
- Keep page JS minimal: calendar navigation, modal open/close/focus, delegated clicks on `data-*` attributes

**Avoid:**
- `fetch` + `JSON.parse` + `innerHTML` / `createElement` to assemble table rows or action buttons
- Embedding HTML/SVG in JSON for client-side assembly
- Global JS helpers that duplicate templ components (`createIconActionLink`, `window.actionIcons`, etc.)

**When JSON is still OK:** lightweight read-only data for widgets that genuinely need client-side state (e.g. calendar date→count summaries), not for markup that templ can render.

## URLs

Always use `utils.URL("/path")`: prepends `/zion-english-admin` in local dev.

## Currency and amount fields

Use `@CurrencyAmountField` from `currency_amount.templ` whenever a form collects currency + amount together. Do not stack separate currency and amount `.form-group` blocks.

```templ
@CurrencyAmountField(CurrencyAmountFieldParams{
	Label:             "Amount",
	AmountID:          "amount",
	AmountName:        "amount",
	CurrencyID:        "currency",
	CurrencyName:      "currency",
	CurrencyValue:     "PHP",
	PlaceholderAmount: "0.00",
	Required:          true,
})
```

For two unrelated fields side by side (not currency+amount), use `.form-row` from `global.templ`.

## HTMX wire constants

Repeated HTMX attribute **values** live in [`frontend/htmx_attrs.go`](frontend/htmx_attrs.go).

- Templates reference constants: `hx-swap={ HxSwapInnerHTML }`, not `hx-swap="innerHTML"`.
- **Exception:** inline `<script>` blocks keep literal wire strings (same rule as enum literals in scripts).
- Custom triggers with event names (e.g. `scheduleRefresh from:body`) stay literal; only shared swap/trigger/target-this **values** are constantized.
- `hx-target` element IDs stay literal (page-specific DOM).
- Prefer existing components ([`dropdowns.templ`](dropdowns.templ), [`pagination.templ`](pagination.templ)) over duplicating attribute combos.

## HTMX Forms

```templ
<form hx-post={ utils.URL("/process") } hx-target="#results" hx-swap={ HxSwapInnerHTML }>
```

Dropdowns load via HTMX on page load: `hx-get`, `hx-trigger="load"`, `hx-target="this"`.

## CSS

CSS variables in `:root` (`global.templ`). Page-specific styles in inline `<style>` blocks.

## Design system

Admin UI uses **cool slate neutrals** with a **Zion green primary** (`#90C020`). Avoid warm beige, cream, or yellow-brown tones on surfaces and borders: not on the brand green.

### Color tokens (`global.templ` `:root`)

| Token | Role |
|-------|------|
| `--color-primary` / `--color-primary-hover` | Primary buttons, time pills, focus ring (Zion green) |
| `--color-primary-light` | Subtle green-tinted headers (e.g. modal detail cards) |
| `--color-background` | Page background (cool gray, not cream) |
| `--color-surface` | Cards, modals, inputs |
| `--color-muted` | Secondary surfaces, table stripes |
| `--color-muted-foreground` | Labels, hints, meta text |
| `--color-border` / `--color-border-subtle` | Borders and dividers |
| `--color-success` / `--color-success-bg` | Conducted / active status |
| `--color-info` / `--color-info-bg` | Rate pills, informational badges |
| `--color-warning` / `--color-warning-bg` | Pending / rescheduled status |
| `--color-destructive` | Delete, cancel-class, errors |

Default assigned colors: `constants.DefaultAssignedColor` (`#90C020`) and `constants.DefaultTeacherAssignedColor` (`#B9D283`). Use these constants: do not hardcode hex in handlers or templates.

### Pills

- **Time** → `@TimeRangePill` (`PillTonePrimary`, green tint)
- **Rate** → `@RatePill` (`PillToneInfo`, sky tint)
- **Status** → `@StatusPill` with domain-specific `PillTone`
- Pill border: `var(--pill-border)` (matches `--color-border`, not hardcoded black)

### Modals

- Overlay: cool slate scrim (`rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.5)`)
- Dialog: white surface, `--color-border`, `--shadow-lg`
- Dismiss: `btn btn-secondary`; primary/destructive: `btn` / `btn-danger`
- Footer: put action buttons as **direct children** of `.modal-footer` so global `gap` and `margin-top: 0` apply. Do not wrap buttons in an extra div unless that wrapper is also a flex row with `gap`.
- Scheduled-class detail summary: `@ScheduledClassDetailCard`: white card with green-tinted header gradient; date/time/rate in a 3-column meta grid (stacks on mobile). Styles live in `global.templ`, not per-modal `<style>` blocks.

### Do not

- Use `background: var(--color-muted)` for primary content cards when a clean white surface is intended
- Hardcode hex colors in templates/handlers when a semantic token or `constants` value exists
- Duplicate global button/pill/modal styles in feature-specific `<style>` blocks

### Button and control alignment

Global `button, .btn` sets `margin-top: var(--space-5)`; `.add-btn` does not. Mixed button rows (modal footers, card actions, toolbars) misalign easily. Follow `ui-button-alignment.mdc` when adding footers, action rows, or controls beside `.icon-action-btn`.

### Inline chip remove buttons

Global `button` styles in `global.templ` set `margin-top`, padding, `display: inline-block`, and filled backgrounds. Any small remove/close control inside a chip, tag, or pill **must** override those defaults or the × will sit below the label.

Prefer the global chip-remove reset in `global.templ` (`button.lm-tag-chip-remove`, `button.chip-remove`, etc.). Per-page fallback pattern:

```css
.chip-remove {
	display: inline-flex;
	align-items: center;
	justify-content: center;
	width: 1.125rem;
	height: 1.125rem;
	padding: 0;
	margin: 0;
	margin-top: 0;
	border: none;
	border-radius: var(--radius-full);
	background: transparent;
	background-color: transparent;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	line-height: 1;
}
.chip-remove:hover {
	background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
	background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
}
```

Parent chip/tag container: `display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: …`.

When adding a new chip UI, copy this pattern: do not rely on bare `button { padding: 0 }` alone.
